**Currently allowed origins** (worker/src/index.ts, `cors({ origin: ... })` middleware, line ~20): `http://localhost:4200`, any `*.pages.dev`, any `*.workers.dev`.

**To add a new custom domain**, edit the `origin` function in `worker/src/index.ts`:

```ts
origin: (origin) => {
  if (!origin) return null;
  if (
    origin === 'http://localhost:4200' ||
    origin.endsWith('.pages.dev') ||
    origin.endsWith('.workers.dev') ||
    origin === 'https://your-custom-domain.com'   // add here
  ) {
    return origin;
  }
  return null;
},
```

Note: Hono's `cors()` treats array entries as exact-match strings, so wildcard/suffix matching requires this function form (per `docs/DEPLOYMENT_NOTES.md` §4). No other file needs changes for CORS itself — though if the frontend is served from the new domain, also update `frontend/src/environments/environment.prod.ts` (`apiUrl`) if the Worker's own domain changes too.
